---
title: Passes API
description: Constructor options and runtime methods for render, compute, and feedback passes.
order: 30
sidebar:
  label: "Passes API"
---

Pass classes are framework-neutral and exported from root, core, and adapter entrypoints.

## Shared render-pass options

`ShaderPass`, `BlitPass`, and `CopyPass` share:

| Option | Default |
| --- | --- |
| `label` | — |
| `enabled` | `true` |
| `needsSwap` | `true` |
| `input` | `'source'` |
| `output` | `'target'` when swapping, otherwise `'source'` |
| `clear` | `false` |
| `clearColor` | `[0, 0, 0, 1]` |
| `preserve` | `true` |
| `filter` | `'linear'` |

`needsSwap: true` is valid only for `source → target`. `canvas` is output-only. Named slots must exist and be written before use.

## `ShaderPass`

Requires `fragment` containing:

```wgsl
fn shade(inputColor: vec4f, uv: vec2f) -> vec4f
```

Public methods:

```ts
setFragment(fragment: string): void
getFragment(): string
```

`setFragment` validates the source contract, then starts asynchronous preparation for active target
formats. The last-known-good pipeline stays active until the newest source compiles. A failed edit is
reported as recoverable; it does not replace the current output.

`shade` and any helper it calls can read the current pass coordinates from `spektralFragment.uv`. The existing `uv` parameter remains required.

## `BlitPass` and `CopyPass`

`BlitPass` samples its input with the configured filter. `CopyPass` attempts a direct GPU copy and otherwise uses an internal blit. Direct copy requires no clear, preserved output, distinct non-canvas textures, and equal dimensions and formats.

Both expose `setSize`, `render`, and `dispose` through the render-pass lifecycle.

## `ComputePass`

```ts
new ComputePass({
	label?: string,
	compute: string,
	workgroupSize?: [number, number?, number?],
	resources?: ComputeResourceMap,
	dispatch?: tuple | 'auto' | (context) => [number, number, number],
	enabled?: boolean
})
```

The source requires `@compute`, `@workgroup_size(...)`, a `compute` function, and `@builtin(global_invocation_id)` in its signature. Literal dimensions are inferred. Set `workgroupSize` when WGSL uses an override or non-literal constant expression; it must match literal WGSL when both are present.

`resources` is keyed by WGSL alias. An omitted map is equivalent to `{}`; no material storage resource is injected implicitly.

```ts
type ComputeResourceDescriptor =
	| {
			texture: string | ComputeExternalTextureReference | ComputeExternalTextureViewReference;
			access: 'sampled';
			view?: ComputeTextureViewDescriptor;
			version?: 'current' | 'initial';
			pingPong?: 'read';
	  }
	| {
			texture: string | ComputeExternalTextureReference | ComputeExternalTextureViewReference;
			access: 'storage-write';
			view?: ComputeTextureViewDescriptor;
			pingPong?: 'write';
	  }
	| {
			buffer: string | ComputeExternalBufferReference;
			access: 'storage-read';
			version?: 'current' | 'initial';
	  }
	| {
			buffer: string | ComputeExternalBufferReference;
			access: 'storage-read-write';
	  }
	| { sampler: string | ComputeExternalSamplerReference };
```

Texture views support `baseMipLevel`, `mipLevelCount`, `baseArrayLayer`, and `arrayLayerCount: 1`. String references are material keys. External references are borrowed typed objects with a stable `resourceId`; see [Compute Shaders](/docs/compute-shaders#borrowed-webgpu-resources) for their metadata and ownership contract.

```ts
setCompute(source, { workgroupSize? }): void
setDispatch(dispatch): void
getCompute(): string
getResources(): ComputeResourceMap
getWorkgroupSize(): [number, number, number]
resolveDispatch(context): [number, number, number]
dispose(): void
```

`isCompute` is a readonly `true` discriminant for inspection. It is not an extension point: custom
compute objects are rejected by the render graph.

`label` is optional and immutable. Diagnostics and graph snapshots use it when present, otherwise
they derive a deterministic label from the pass kind and declaration index.

## `PingPongComputePass`

Requires `resources`, accepts a positive-integer `iterations` (default `1`), and adds the `isPingPong` discriminant. The map must contain exactly one sampled `pingPong: 'read'` descriptor and one storage-write `pingPong: 'write'` descriptor. Both point to the same storage texture.

```ts
new PingPongComputePass({
	label: 'Velocity iterations',
	compute,
	resources: {
		previous: { texture: 'velocity', access: 'sampled', pingPong: 'read' },
		next: { texture: 'velocity', access: 'storage-write', pingPong: 'write' },
		obstacles: { texture: 'obstacles', access: 'sampled' }
	},
	iterations: 8,
	dispatch: 'auto'
});
```

The renderer keeps A/B names and parity private. It publishes the latest result under the logical material key after the iteration batch.

`workgroupSize` has the same override/non-literal behavior as `ComputePass`.

```ts
setIterations(count): void
setCompute(source, { workgroupSize? }): void
setDispatch(dispatch): void
getIterations(): number
getCompute(): string
getResources(): ComputeResourceMap
getWorkgroupSize(): [number, number, number]
resolveDispatch(context): [number, number, number]
dispose(): void
```

## `PingPongShaderPass`

Runs a pre-scene fragment shader with `fn frag(uv: vec2f) -> vec4f`. `target` must be a declared, fragment-visible, non-storage material texture.

| Option | Default |
| --- | --- |
| `label` | — |
| `width`, `height` | Canvas axis multiplied by `scale` |
| `scale` | `1` |
| `format` | `'rgba16float'` |
| `filter` | `'linear'` |
| `addressModeU/V` | `'clamp-to-edge'` |
| `iterations` | `1` |
| `clearColor` | `[0, 0, 0, 0]` |
| `defines`, `includes` | `{}` |
| `enabled` | `true` |

Dimensions and scale must be finite and positive, iterations a positive integer, and format float-sampled.

```ts
setFragment(fragment, { defines?, includes? }?): void
setIterations(count): void
setDimensions(width?, height?): void
setScale(scale): void
reset(clearColor?): void
consumeResetColor(): RGBA | null
getCurrentOutput(): string
advanceFrame(): void
resolveSize(canvasSize): { width, height }
getTarget(): string
getFragment(): string
getFragmentLineMap(): MaterialLineMap
getIterations(): number
getFormat(): GPUTextureFormat
getFilter(): GPUFilterMode
getAddressModeU(): GPUAddressMode
getAddressModeV(): GPUAddressMode
getClearColor(): RGBA
dispose(): void
```

`isPingPongShader` is a readonly `true` discriminant for inspection, not a structural extension
point. `setDimensions`, `setScale`, and `reset` request A/B reinitialization;
`consumeResetColor` is renderer-facing and clears that pending request.

When a pass instance is shared by multiple canvases, each renderer's texture pair has independent
iteration and reset state. `reset()` applies to every pair on its next render.
`getCurrentOutput()` reports the A/B key for the most recently rendered pair.

Custom `RenderPass` objects may also expose a readonly `label?: string`. Spektral uses the same
labeling rule for built-in and custom passes.

`frag` and its helper functions can read the ping-pong target coordinates from `spektralFragment.uv`. They use the pass target dimensions and the same public Y-up orientation as the `uv` parameter.

See [Render Passes](/docs/render-passes) and [Compute Shaders](/docs/compute-shaders).
